   {
    "reason": "Same missing-root condition. Apply also edits openspec/ files on purpose (ticking tasks), so an unconditional ban on writing under openspec/ would be wrong. The condition can't be written as a predicate.",
    "statement": "ap-014"
   },
   {
    "reason": "Same missing-root condition. 'A command that creates the root' as a side effect can't be told apart from legitimate openspec writes when the root already exists.",
    "statement": "ap-015"
   },
   {
    "reason": "Only applies when the CLI returns state \"blocked\". The CLI output state isn't something the reference language can observe, so it can't be an applies_when predicate.",
    "statement": "ap-023"
   },
   {
    "reason": "Only applies when state is blocked and missingArtifacts is non-empty in the CLI JSON. Neither is observable in the predicate language.",
